ressbook><name>NISHIMURA KEIJI</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>TOSAKA AKIO</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>UMINO SHIGERU</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>HAYASHI, HIROMASA</name></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>KYONO, KAZUAKI</name></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>NISHIMURA, KEIJI</name></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>TOSAKA, AKIO</name></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>UMINO, SHIGERU</name></addressbook></inventor></inventors></parties></bibliographic-data><abstract load-source="docdb" source="national office" status="new" lang="EN"><p>A sufficient inner oxidized layer can be formed on the ferrite surface layers of steel plates, regardless of steel constituent elements and a production history and despite radiation heating such as radiant tubes used in recrystallization annealing before hot-dipping, by heat-treating, after hot-rolling, blank billets with black scales deposited thereon in a reduction-restricted atmosphere and a temperature range of 650 to 950 DEG.C, thereby it is possible to impart an excellent hot-dipping and chemical conversion treating features to plating steel plates.</p></abstract><abstract load-source="docdb" source="national office" status="new" lang="FR"><p>L'invention concerne la formation d'une couche à oxydation interne suffisante sur les couches de surface ferritiques de plaques d'acier, en dépit des éléments constituants de l'acier et des antécédents de production et malgré le chauffage par rayonnement tel que celui des tubes chauffants utilisés dans le recuit de régénération avant l'immersion à chaud. On effectue un traitement à chaud, après laminage à chaud, de billettes de flan sur lesquelles sont déposées des calamines noires, dans une atmosphère de restriction de réduction et à une température comprise entre 650 et 950  DEG C. Grâce à l'invention, il est possible de doter des plaques d'acier de revêtement d'excellentes caractéristiques d'immersion à chaud et de traitement par conversion chimique.</p></abstract><copyright>User acknowledges that the Information Retrieval Facility (IRF) and its third party providers retain all right, title and interest in and to this xml under applicable copyright laws. User acquires no ownership rights to this xml including but not limited to its format. User hereby accepts the terms and conditions of the Licence Agreement set forth at http://www.ir-facility.org/legal/marec/data_licence</copyright></patent-document>